      "lo": "lo:pp3u7-1-1",
      "label": "Define set of zeroes",
      "statements": [
        {
          "id": "pp3u7-1:definition-1",
          "type": "definition",
          "text": "0, 1 and 2 are called the set of zeroes of the function.",
          "page": 15
        },
        {
          "id": "pp3u7-1:definition-2",
          "type": "definition",
          "text": "If $f:\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is a polynomial in x, then the set of values of x which makes $f(x)=0$ is called the set of zeroes of the function f and is denoted by the symbol $Z(f)$. Formula: $Z(f)=\\{x: f(x)=0\\}$",
          "page": 15
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "lo": "lo:pp3u7-1-2",
      "label": "Find set of zeroes",
      "statements": [
        {
          "id": "pp3u7-1:rule-1",
          "type": "rule",
          "text": "Z(f) is the solution set of the equation f(x) = 0.",
          "page": 15
        },
        {
          "id": "pp3u7-1:method-1",
          "type": "method",
          "text": "To get the zeros of the function f, put f(x) = 0 and solve the resulting equation to find the set of values of x.",
          "page": 15
        }
      ]
    },
